  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 139 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nWhile the extended forecast is expected to remain largely quiet, \nseveral passing synoptic features traversing the CONUS will bring \nperiods of cloudiness. The first of these features is a positively \ntilted trough forecast to be oriented from the Great Lakes into the \nDesert Southwest. While precipitation is not expected due to a deep \nlayer of dry ambient air, high-level clouds are forecast to stream \nacross the region. Otherwise, the area will remain sandwiched \nbetween passing shortwaves to both the north and south while staying \ndry. Temperatures will run above normal through the period, with \ndaytime highs in the upper 50s to lower 60s and overnight lows \nsettling into the upper 30s to lower 40s.",
